-- EXPECT-ERROR: contains a non-exhaustive `match`, which panics at runtime
-- Capabilities widening, Task 6 (F3) -- `cap no_panic`
-- (`check_no_panic_module`, `typecheck.ml`), the REJECT side for the
-- match-non-exhaustiveness panic surface. A non-exhaustive `match` lowers to a
-- runtime "no matching clause" panic, so a `cap no_panic` module must reject it
-- just like an explicit `panic` (see reject/t42).
--
-- `check_exhaustiveness` (`typecheck.ml`) already finds every non-exhaustive
-- match and, besides emitting the usual Warning, records the offending
-- `match`'s span into `env.nonexhaustive_match_spans` (a shared ref).
-- `check_no_panic_module` -- which runs ONLY for `cap no_panic` modules --
-- reads that side-table and, for any recorded span nested (by `span_within`
-- containment) inside one of THIS module's own function bodies, reports an
-- ERROR. A non-exhaustive match in a PLAIN module stays a non-blocking Warning
-- (see accept/t14). See core-march-types.md §2.8.11.
mod Guarded do
  cap no_panic

  fn get(opt : Option(Int)) : Int do
    match opt do
      Some(x) -> x
    end
  end
end
